{"title":"2015 EGMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an acute-angled triangle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> The angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and meets the circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2920fa2bc40ed68149a854f8b32c09f619b0d70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fefa4180653d8e0aa4bbc7e507fd4636f1425412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADF = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455ee52a9ab7dd830f0d1c3249ff02ae5e181f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega .$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A domino is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e03b602154bf17643e7945df4dae9dcd3a22081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c8b62c658c4d2cde679951a8b1e450d1b88b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times  2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> tile. Determine in how many ways exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> dominoes can be placed without overlapping on a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fc2c579d6302d826e12b8b996f27c03480e07b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n \\times  2n$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> chessboard so that every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times  2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> square contains at least two uncovered unit squares which lie in the same row or column.\t\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5be19edae9196ae8f8106e8133e0bf69ca909c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n, m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> be integers greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d717ffa9458b2e7e7584a4a1938091a7660121c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" /> be positive integers not greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/11635427dac1ad5c3e57beb5e3dfcb329a78248b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^m$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that there exist positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd35bca8bfcba6465c5f56fc73a7dd9b9b7ce511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> not greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb0edea7d27206dc42c824f5566800b5e428083.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(a_1 + b_1, a_2 + b_2, \\dots, a_m + b_m) &lt; n,\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948c9a3eab1d7b70c1aecb5780104f1f4aa48638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the greatest common divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/76478e7f08df53972172ae2c46f92a500fa9ee59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine whether there exists an infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745b81add053aa31f45d72cb9a898e3441e74bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> of positive integers\nwhich satisfies the equality<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0929d4f9aa69797c71294b2c26c0dded433e8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+2}=a_{n+1}+\\sqrt{a_{n+1}+a_{n}}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> be positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cce1bd621aff652b0983cbc94a24545e5f4bdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. Anastasia partitions the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/48981f465adf2b2993849ca2d973677fab69ce1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\dots , 2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> pairs. Boris then chooses one integer from each pair and finds the sum of these chosen integers.\nProve that Anastasia can select the pairs so that Boris cannot make his sum equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the orthocentre and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the centroid of acute-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c7105fb704dc1248590ad440c598e0f08a5afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\ne AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0fb91a035ffe48a96fc69a4a82b850f841f709b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43af75e68e4891596da73589c31604f5a52e5397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG = GP&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_EGMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 EGMO Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 237/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8154/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23583:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060800 and revision id 184633. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}